  "limits": "Numerical screen under declared hypotheses, uncorrelated with any build or measurement. The body is the study twin (1 scan unit = 1 mm by owner instruction; unobserved geometry closed by hypotheses), blocked into cubes: walls and gaps thinner than the pitch are merged or lost, and the stair-step exterior area does not converge to the surface area. With a Biot number near 1e-3 the mean temperature follows h*A/(rho*cp*V), so the difference between the two pitches is a difference of discrete area and volume, not a discretisation error estimate. Cell-mean von Mises values sit at re-entrant voxel corners where the elastic solution is singular; they are reported as solver output, not as stresses, and their maximum must not be quoted as a margin. Uniform 500 K start, h = 20 W/m2K, clamped lowest face, elastic constants and the AlSi10Mg-class properties are assumptions. No laser, layer deposition, powder bed, residual-stress build-up, support, distortion compensation, porosity or microstructure is modelled. Nothing here establishes printability, material, dimensional accuracy or function."
